<title>GERMANY: BASF fertiliser unit turns profit - paper.</title>
<headline>BASF fertiliser unit turns profit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>BASF AG said its fertilizer business, a former problem child at the German chemicals group, returned to making a profit in 1996, a German newspaper reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung quoted Dieter Thomaschewski, leader of the BASF fertilizer unit, as saying the subsidiary had reduced its fixed costs while also reporting higher sales that led to a profit.</p>
<p>He said the unit had sales of more than two billion marks, up from 1.9 billion marks in 1995.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
